<h1 class="article-title">Decisions Adopted by the Liepāja SEZ Board on 18 March</h1>
<div class="block_text mt-5 mb-4">
<div class="row">
<div class="col"><div class="col-12 output"><h6>2024. gada 18. martā notika kārtējā Liepājas speciālās ekonomiskās zonas (Liepājas SEZ) valdes sēde, kurā  izskatīja un atbalstīja Liepājas SEZ kapitālsabiedrības statusa piešķiršanu SIA “AE Partner”, trīs Liepājas SEZ kapitālsabiedrību ieguldījumu projektus par kopējo summu 5,41 milj. EUR, pieņēma lēmumus par nekustamo īpašumu pirmpirkuma tiesībām un precizēja ilgtermiņa nomas līgumu. Tāpat Liepājas SEZ valde nolēma iestāties biedrībā “WindEurope”.</h6><p>Liepāja SEZ company status</p><p>To continue growing and implement the investment project “Construction of a New Production and Administrative Building at 1/3 Ganību Street, Liepāja”, AE Partner decided to enter into an agreement to conduct business in the Liepāja Special Economic Zone and become a Liepāja SEZ company.</p><p>AE Partner is a Danish-owned company operating in Liepāja since 2003. In recent years its output and turnover have increased significantly, with annual turnover exceeding EUR 74 million. It is one of Liepāja’s largest employers, employing 540 people. The company produces high-quality automation systems and designs and manufactures electrical panels. It plans to expand production, build a new facility and create new jobs.</p><p>The Board decided to grant AE Partner Liepāja SEZ company status and conclude an investment agreement for the period from 1 April 2024 to 31 December 2025.</p><p>AE Partner owner Klaus Ravn said: “I am very grateful that this support will allow us to continue growing and creating good jobs in Liepāja.”</p><p> </p><p>Implementation of investment projects</p><p>The Board considered and supported two additional investment projects by Liepāja SEZ companies, totalling EUR 440,241.55:</p><ul><li>PUMAC LIEPAJA, a Liepāja SEZ company, plans the project “Landscaping and Creation of Car Parking Spaces for a Tenant” from 1 April to 31 December 2024, with a total value of EUR 156,166.00.</li><li>Vecās Ostmalas Biznesa Parks, a Liepāja SEZ company, plans the project “Combining Production Premises and Adapting Them for the Tenant’s Business Activities” from 25 March to 31 December 2024, for EUR 251,093.78.</li></ul><p>In 2023, the Liepāja SEZ Authority concluded 15 investment agreements with SEZ companies, with planned investments totalling EUR 5,481,903.28. In 2024, the Board supported and concluded three investment projects worth a total of EUR 4,129,605.00.</p><p>Maintenance of depths in port waters. To ensure safe navigation in the Port of Liepāja, the Board reviewed and approved plans for maintaining shipping channels in 2024 and decided to conclude a contract with UAB Green Line Shipping for maintaining channel and harbour-basin depths. The company was selected through procurement after submitting the most economically advantageous tender at the lowest price.</p><p>Amendments to a cooperation agreement. As part of the first stage of the Liepāja Industrial Park development project and in accordance with the agreement concluded with the Central Finance and Contracting Agency, the Board decided to amend its cooperation agreement of 27 April 2023 with Liepājas ūdens. The amendments clarify work on three street sections, including street infrastructure and lighting, external water-supply networks, domestic sewerage, heating networks, external electrical networks and customer electricity connections.</p><p>Planned activities. The Board decided not to approve the part of DG Termināls’ proposed new waste recovery activity involving construction and installation of a rubber and plastic waste pyrolysis plant. After evaluating the environmental impact assessment (EIA), its findings and conditions, the interests of local residents and existing and planned polluting activities under the permit, the proposed activity was found unacceptable from environmental and public-interest perspectives.</p><p>The Board stressed that the assessment must address not only environmental impacts but also human health, safety and cumulative risks to surrounding infrastructure. The EIA did not sufficiently detail measures in the event of accidents or adequately assess impacts on the environment, health and life in such events. Rights of first refusal: the Board also decided not to exercise its rights of first refusal over the property at 117 Brīvības Street and a one-fifth undivided share of properties at 117A and 121B Brīvības Street, Liepāja.</p><p>The Board also decided not to exercise its right of first refusal over the property at 35A Jaunā ostmala, Liepāja.</p><p>Membership of WindEurope. Since 2022, the Liepāja SEZ Authority has worked actively to establish an important renewable-energy industry centre in the Port of Liepāja. The Liepāja SEZ Development Plan and the city’s spatial plan envisage development of the Outer Harbour area for port terminals.</p><p>WindEurope is one of the industry’s leading organisations, bringing together major companies and supporting information exchange and joint policy development. The Board decided to join WindEurope to strengthen the Port of Liepāja’s competitiveness and international visibility and create conditions for a new industry to develop in Liepāja and the region.</p><p>WindEurope promotes the production and use of wind energy in Europe. It has more than 500 members in over 50 countries, including major wind-energy manufacturers, component suppliers, research institutes, national wind and renewable-energy associations, developers, contractors, electricity suppliers, financial firms, insurers and consultants.</p></div>
